    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27210" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δῐονύ̄σ-ιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of Dionysus,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῶρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					<u>Scol.Oxy.Fr.</u>
					1.9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δ., ὁ</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήν</span>), name of month in Aetolia, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				9(1).374
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				524.14
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Crete</span>), <i><span class="en">
				1009.20
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Chalcedon</span>), etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διονύσιον, τό,</span> fruit of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κισσός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				2.179
			</span></i>.</div>
